flowchart TB
    accTitle: The whole app — ask, process, and explore
    accDescr: Follow the numbered connectors. Subnumbers identify branches or smaller steps. Optional actions and supporting relationships are labeled separately. The browser sends questions and recent context to the app server. The server coordinates an AI provider and checked read-only database access. Progress and SQL appear while work continues, followed by an answer, table, or clear error. Schema browsing, cancellation, follow-ups, and local table actions complete the user journey.
    %% Companion guide: docs/architecture.md

    BROWSER["Your workspace: Ask questions or follow up"]:::view
    SERVER["App server: Check requests and coordinate AI"]:::work
    QUERY["Database access: Check and run read-only SQL"]:::work
    RESPONSE["Back in your workspace: Answer, table, warnings, or error"]:::view
    EXPLORE["Explore the loaded rows: Sort, page, resize, or export CSV"]:::view
    MODEL["AI provider: Writes SQL and explains results"]:::work
    DB[("PostgreSQL: Your connected database")]:::data
    SCHEMA["Browse tables and columns: Load or refresh the saved list"]:::data
    LIVE["While waiting: See progress and SQL preview"]:::view
    CANCEL["Cancel the current turn or start a new chat when idle"]:::note

    BROWSER -->|1. Submit question| SERVER
    SERVER -->|2. Query data| QUERY
    QUERY -->|3. Show response| RESPONSE
    RESPONSE -->|4. Explore results| EXPLORE
    SERVER <-->|AI requests and replies| MODEL
    QUERY <-->|SQL and matching rows| DB
    BROWSER -.->|Optional| SCHEMA
    SERVER -.->|While working| LIVE
    BROWSER -.->|Optional| CANCEL

    classDef view fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#172033,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef work fill:#f5f3ff,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#4c1d95,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef data fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef note fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#78350f,stroke-width:1.5px;
